    if (info.code == 0) {
        printf("Error: %s\n", info.message);
    } else {
        printf("Operation successful: %s\n", info.message);
    }
    return 0;
}
```

In this version, the `checkError` function returns a structure that contains both the error code and a message. The `main` function then prints the message based on the error code.

